I'll start by visiting OwnCloud to download the file.
<tool_call>
{"name": "browser_navigate", "arguments": {"url": "http://localhost:8092"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_response>
{"url":"http://localhost:8092/index.php/login","title":"ownCloud","description":"ownCloud login page with username and password fields."}
</tool_response>

<tool_call>
{"name": "browser_click", "arguments": {"selector": "#user"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_response>
{"success":true}
</tool_response>

<tool_call>
{"name": "browser_type", "arguments": {"selector": "#user", "text": "admin"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_response>
{"success":true}
</tool_response>

<tool_call>
{"name": "browser_click", "arguments": {"selector": "#password"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_response>
{"success":true}
</tool_response>

<tool_call>
{"name": "browser_type", "arguments": {"selector": "#password", "text": "admin"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_response>
{"success":true}
</tool_response>

<tool_call>
{"name": "browser_click", "arguments": {"selector": "button[type=submit]"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_response>
{"success":true,"url":"http://localhost:8092/index.php/apps/files/","title":"Files - ownCloud"}
</tool_response>

<tool_call>
{"name": "browser_navigate", "arguments": {"url": "http://localhost:8092/index.php/apps/files/?dir=/Shared/Compliance/Raw%20Logs"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_response>
{"url":"http://localhost:8092/index.php/apps/files/?dir=/Shared/Compliance/Raw%20Logs","title":"Files - ownCloud","description":"ownCloud file manager showing the contents of the 'Raw Logs' directory under 'Shared/Compliance'. The file 'april-attendance-data.csv' is listed."}
</tool_response>

The file is visible. Let me download it via the OwnCloud WebDAV endpoint.
<tool_call>
{"name": "execute_command", "arguments": {"command": "curl -u admin:admin 'http://localhost:8092/remote.php/webdav/Shared/Compliance/Raw%20Logs/april-attendance-data.csv' -o '/workspace/april-attendance-data.csv'"}}
</tool_call>
